1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,923
START DATING...

3
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,958
BETWEEN STEPS

4
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,794
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:43,877 --> 00:00:45,462
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

6
00:00:58,475 --> 00:00:59,601
-[Youjin] Boo!
-You scared me.

7
00:01:00,227 --> 00:01:01,687
[Youjin] I got you.

8
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:03,230
I was just messing with you.

9
00:01:11,196 --> 00:01:13,073
Sorry, I kept you waiting.

10
00:01:26,253 --> 00:01:28,422
I was just trying
to pull a little prank on you.

11
00:01:32,009 --> 00:01:33,260
Did I scare you that badly?

12
00:01:35,721 --> 00:01:37,639
Are you mad?

13
00:01:40,809 --> 00:01:41,852
No.

14
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:44,062
I just...

15
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:46,982
hugged you because I like you.

16
00:01:48,859 --> 00:01:51,028
Because I like you so much.

17
00:02:06,209 --> 00:02:09,713
ONE HUNDRED YEARS OF SOLITUDE 1

18
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:12,215
[Youseong] Mom, is that fun?

19
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:14,509
EPISODE 8

20
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:16,219
I don't know. I'm just reading it.

21
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,221
I felt like reading a book.

22
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:20,515
Did you buy it?

23
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,518
Of course. Would I find it on the street?

24
00:02:24,978 --> 00:02:26,980
I was bored, so I went to the bookstore,

25
00:02:27,064 --> 00:02:28,523
and this one looked interesting.

26
00:02:31,485 --> 00:02:34,529
Is it about how people
are lonely or something?

27
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:39,618
Are you lonely?

28
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,204
Everyone is lonely.

29
00:02:45,082 --> 00:02:48,585
It doesn't matter
if you have a husband or kids.

30
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:54,800
Sometimes I wonder
why my life is the way it is.

31
00:02:54,883 --> 00:02:56,593
It's sad and lonely.

32
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:02,641
Your life is sad and lonely?

33
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:06,019
I don't know.

34
00:03:06,103 --> 00:03:07,270
Maybe it's menopause.

35
00:03:08,063 --> 00:03:12,401
One minute I feel good,
the next I feel awful.

36
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:14,236
I'm hot, then cold.

37
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:16,947
I laugh, then I cry.
I'm all over the place. Jeez.

38
00:03:17,948 --> 00:03:20,242
I don't know. I'm old now.

39
00:03:20,325 --> 00:03:21,743
I'm old.

40
00:03:21,827 --> 00:03:23,120
It's not because you're old.

41
00:03:23,203 --> 00:03:24,871
It's all because of Lim Youjin.

42
00:03:26,248 --> 00:03:28,834
What's wrong with accepting some fruit
from a customer?

43
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:31,253
Who does she think she is
to chew you out like that?

44
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:33,505
Well, that was actually my fault.

45
00:03:34,464 --> 00:03:37,092
I should've known better
than to make a mistake like that.

46
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:38,427
Yeah, exactly.

47
00:03:38,510 --> 00:03:40,387
It was just a mistake. Right?

48
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:43,849
That brat shouldn't cry
and yell at her mom over that.

49
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:45,892
She was probably upset herself.

50
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:49,980
I don't even get
what's so upsetting about it,

51
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:52,983
let alone why she'd throw
such a huge tantrum at you over it.

52
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:55,735
Does she think
she's so sophisticated and classy?

53
00:03:56,445 --> 00:03:58,655
At the end of the day,
she's still your daughter.

54
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:03,160
I can't seem to poop. [sighs]

55
00:04:04,035 --> 00:04:05,662
This is all because of you, Dad.

56
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:07,956
[Yongseok] What is?

57
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:13,253
If you'd bought Mom expensive fruit
and broadened her horizons,

58
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:16,506
she wouldn't be reading
this stupid book now.

59
00:04:18,258 --> 00:04:19,593
What? What book?

60
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:21,678
[Youseong] <i>One Hundred Years of Solitude.</i>

61
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:25,682
Just talking about it
is pissing me off all over again.

62
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:27,809
Hey! Lim Youjin!

63
00:04:27,893 --> 00:04:29,019
Come on out.

64
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:32,189
Your mom is feeling lonely because of you,

65
00:04:32,272 --> 00:04:34,274
and now she is reading this stupid book!

66
00:04:35,192 --> 00:04:36,693
Get out here, you little brat!

67
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:37,819
Be quiet.

68
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:40,197
Youjin isn't even in her room right now.

69
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,281
She's out?

70
00:04:41,865 --> 00:04:43,784
I thought she was home.
When did she leave?

71
00:04:43,867 --> 00:04:45,702
Yeah, she went to the grocery store.

72
00:04:45,786 --> 00:04:47,746
I asked her to get some tofu. [sighs]

73
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:51,458
[Youjin] Are you sure nothing's up?

74
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:53,001
[Minjae] Hmm?

75
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:54,127
No. Nothing's up.

76
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:56,004
[Youjin] Hmm.

77
00:04:56,797 --> 00:04:58,381
Nothing's up,

78
00:04:58,465 --> 00:05:00,884
but you suddenly wanted to see me?

79
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:02,052
Out of nowhere?

80
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:04,137
[Minjae] Yeah.

81
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,807
[Youjin] You like me that much?

82
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:12,229
What's so great about me?

83
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:17,651
Tell me. What is it that you like so much?

84
00:05:19,528 --> 00:05:21,822
Just... everything.

85
00:05:22,572 --> 00:05:26,535
Mmm. No, you have to be specific.
Be specific.

86
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:29,704
[Minjae] Hmm...

87
00:05:31,081 --> 00:05:33,792
[sighs] You're taking
way too long to answer.

88
00:05:37,629 --> 00:05:38,630
You're pretty.

89
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:41,508
I'm pretty. What else?

90
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:42,676
-What else?
-Yeah.

91
00:05:44,719 --> 00:05:45,720
What else?

92
00:05:45,804 --> 00:05:46,805
You're cute.

93
00:05:47,472 --> 00:05:49,099
I'm pretty and cute.

94
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:50,517
-What else?
-What else?

95
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:52,602
[Minjae] Hmm.

96
00:05:52,686 --> 00:05:53,854
You're nice.

97
00:05:54,688 --> 00:05:57,148
I'm pretty, cute, and nice.

98
00:05:57,232 --> 00:05:58,275
What else?

99
00:05:58,358 --> 00:05:59,359
[chuckles softly] More?

100
00:06:00,569 --> 00:06:02,445
Well, you only said three things.

101
00:06:02,529 --> 00:06:04,364
That I'm pretty, cute, and nice.

102
00:06:05,073 --> 00:06:06,533
Come on, keep going.

103
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:08,618
Keep going? Just keep going?

104
00:06:08,702 --> 00:06:09,786
Yeah.

105
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:12,414
Come on, I'm asking you
to write a thesis, am I?

106
00:06:12,497 --> 00:06:15,000
You should have enough
for two to three pages.

107
00:06:15,667 --> 00:06:16,668
Is that so hard?

108
00:06:17,586 --> 00:06:19,754
[Minjae] Hmm.

109
00:06:22,841 --> 00:06:23,925
Well... What about you?

110
00:06:24,009 --> 00:06:25,010
[Youjin] Hmm?

111
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:28,013
I mean, there must be things
you like about me too.

112
00:06:28,096 --> 00:06:30,724
Go ahead and fill two pages.

113
00:06:33,435 --> 00:06:34,853
[Youjin] Hmm...

114
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:39,274
You're taking a while too.

115
00:06:42,903 --> 00:06:44,362
I can't say anything.

116
00:06:44,446 --> 00:06:46,072
Because I don't like you.

117
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:48,658
Huh?

118
00:06:50,368 --> 00:06:51,369
What?

119
00:06:54,164 --> 00:06:55,832
What are you talking about?

120
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:57,626
You said you liked me.

121
00:06:58,585 --> 00:06:59,586
When did I say that?

122
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:03,882
You said you liked me before.

123
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:09,095
When did I say I liked you?

124
00:07:09,179 --> 00:07:10,388
I said I loved you.

125
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:19,105
I love you.

126
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:21,191
Me too.

127
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:26,196
Hey...

128
00:07:27,572 --> 00:07:30,033
Hey, we're in public. Don't.

129
00:07:30,116 --> 00:07:32,702
What? You've never kissed
in public before?

130
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:35,246
[softly] Come on, don't.

131
00:07:35,330 --> 00:07:38,124
-Are you embarrassed? Your ears are red.
-Come on, stop it.

132
00:07:38,208 --> 00:07:39,209
Why?

133
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:40,502
Stop it.

134
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:42,545
Come on, what if someone sees us?
[chuckles awkwardly] Stop.

135
00:07:44,798 --> 00:07:47,175
Wait, are you mad?

136
00:07:47,801 --> 00:07:49,386
You're even cuter when you're mad.

137
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:52,347
Don't say I'm cute. I'm older than you.

138
00:07:54,516 --> 00:07:55,892
You're so cute.

139
00:07:55,975 --> 00:07:57,644
You're so cute, I want to bite you.

140
00:07:57,727 --> 00:07:58,728
Nom!

141
00:07:58,812 --> 00:08:00,063
Don't bite. Don't bite me.

142
00:08:00,146 --> 00:08:01,481
-I want to.
-Don't bite me.

143
00:08:01,564 --> 00:08:03,441
-I want to bite you.
-It'll hurt. Stop it.

144
00:08:03,525 --> 00:08:05,068
-Come on, come here.
-Stop it.

145
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:06,403
Nobody's watching.

146
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:08,154
-[cellphone vibrating]
-You're getting a call. Answer it.

147
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:10,073
What? Who's calling me?

148
00:08:11,616 --> 00:08:12,617
Mom?

149
00:08:13,868 --> 00:08:14,869
I'll be quiet.

150
00:08:16,371 --> 00:08:17,789
Mom. What's up?

151
00:08:19,416 --> 00:08:20,417
Tofu?

152
00:08:21,876 --> 00:08:23,169
Ah...

153
00:08:23,253 --> 00:08:24,629
The convenience store was out,

154
00:08:24,713 --> 00:08:26,798
so I came to the supermarket
on the main road.

155
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:28,883
You could've just come back
if they were out.

156
00:08:28,967 --> 00:08:30,385
You didn't have to go that far.

157
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:34,556
Well, I was wondering

158
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:37,434
why it was taking you so long
just to get some tofu.

159
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:38,727
Yeah.

160
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:39,894
I sent Youseong over.

161
00:08:39,978 --> 00:08:41,020
You haven't seen him?

162
00:08:41,104 --> 00:08:42,188
Youseong?

163
00:08:43,565 --> 00:08:45,692
I haven't seen him.

164
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:47,986
Yeah.

165
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:49,571
Oh...

166
00:08:50,822 --> 00:08:52,198
I bought the tofu.

167
00:08:52,282 --> 00:08:53,283
Yeah.

168
00:08:53,908 --> 00:08:56,578
Uh... I'm nearby. I'll be home soon.

169
00:08:56,661 --> 00:08:57,704
I'm on my way now.

170
00:08:58,663 --> 00:08:59,998
Yeah, in the alley.

171
00:09:00,874 --> 00:09:02,792
Well, in like two to three minutes?

172
00:09:04,461 --> 00:09:05,795
-[Minjae mouthing] Are you leaving? Okay.
-Yeah.

173
00:09:06,421 --> 00:09:07,422
[Minjae mouthing] Go. Go ahead.

174
00:09:08,173 --> 00:09:09,591
-[door bell chimes]
-[Youjin] Yeah.

175
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:10,884
I already bought it.

176
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:13,595
-[door bell chimes]
-[Youjin speaking indistinctly]

177
00:09:50,799 --> 00:09:53,093
We've met at school before, right?

178
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,261
Yes.

179
00:09:56,387 --> 00:09:58,056
What brings you to our neighborhood?

180
00:09:59,766 --> 00:10:01,434
I was just...

181
00:10:01,518 --> 00:10:02,811
[Youseong] Are you here to meet Youjin?

182
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:07,440
Yes.

183
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:10,777
So, what's your relationship with Youjin?

184
00:10:11,736 --> 00:10:12,737
Boyfriend?

185
00:10:13,488 --> 00:10:14,489
[Minjae] Pardon?

186
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:17,325
Are you two dating?

187
00:10:19,327 --> 00:10:20,787
Yes, we're dating.

188
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,872
-We're serious about our relationship.
-[Youseong sighs]

189
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:25,458
[tuts] Serious?

190
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:30,296
We're seriously and genuinely dating.

191
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:31,381
Since when?

192
00:10:31,464 --> 00:10:35,885
Well, we first met last fall.

193
00:10:35,969 --> 00:10:38,304
But we parted ways
without even exchanging names.

194
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:40,723
Then we met again this year...

195
00:10:40,807 --> 00:10:42,433
So you've been together since then?

196
00:10:42,934 --> 00:10:44,602
No, not really.

197
00:10:45,562 --> 00:10:47,564
We only started
officially dating recently.

198
00:10:47,647 --> 00:10:50,066
So if you only just started dating,

199
00:10:50,150 --> 00:10:52,235
I guess you two
haven't gotten that far yet.

200
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:55,738
Pardon?

201
00:10:55,822 --> 00:10:57,657
Come on, quit playing dumb.

202
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:01,786
Did you mess around
with my sister or not, you little punk?

203
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:05,373
Gosh, seriously.

204
00:11:09,711 --> 00:11:13,673
First off, our family
is extremely conservative and strict.

205
00:11:13,756 --> 00:11:15,341
It's basically the Joseon dynasty.

206
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:18,678
Oh...

207
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:22,015
So even if you two are dating,
don't cross any lines, okay?

208
00:11:22,557 --> 00:11:24,809
Keep it wholesome and innocent.

209
00:11:28,938 --> 00:11:30,857
You can look at her, but don't touch.

210
00:11:33,693 --> 00:11:35,111
Aren't you going to answer me?

211
00:11:35,195 --> 00:11:37,405
Yeah, sure. I understand. Yeah.

212
00:11:37,989 --> 00:11:40,200
And don't stay out too late, okay?

213
00:11:40,283 --> 00:11:43,453
When the clock hits 10 p.m.,
you bring her straight home.

214
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:46,956
Okay.

215
00:11:48,458 --> 00:11:50,001
So does that mean you approve?

216
00:11:50,084 --> 00:11:52,003
You're okay with me dating Youjin?

217
00:11:52,086 --> 00:11:53,755
Well, I'm not her mom or dad.

218
00:11:53,838 --> 00:11:55,757
It's not my place
to approve or disapprove.

219
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:58,551
I'm just laying down some ground rules.

220
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:00,553
[Minjae] Okay. I understand.

221
00:12:07,018 --> 00:12:10,104
By the way, I have a question.

222
00:12:10,188 --> 00:12:12,440
Sure, go ahead. You can ask me anything.

223
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:16,110
I heard you had trouble with your leg,

224
00:12:17,362 --> 00:12:18,696
but it looks fine.

225
00:12:20,448 --> 00:12:23,576
Was it from a car accident or something?

226
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:26,079
Oh, it wasn't a car accident.

227
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:29,707
I had surgery because I had osteosarcoma.

228
00:12:29,791 --> 00:12:31,084
Osteosarcoma?

229
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:32,669
What kind of disease is that?

230
00:12:33,253 --> 00:12:36,047
It's a tumor that develops in the bone
or around a joint.

231
00:12:37,048 --> 00:12:38,049
So...

232
00:12:38,883 --> 00:12:41,427
I had part of it amputated.

233
00:12:42,845 --> 00:12:43,846
What?

234
00:12:45,682 --> 00:12:48,601
Wait, by "amputated," you mean...

235
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:52,313
They cut off your leg?

236
00:12:54,649 --> 00:12:56,734
But your leg...

237
00:12:56,818 --> 00:13:00,905
Uh... I'm missing my right leg
below the knee.

238
00:13:00,989 --> 00:13:03,616
I use a prosthetic leg to get around.

239
00:13:05,076 --> 00:13:06,411
Oh...

240
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:09,497
Oh... I get it.

241
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:12,917
I'm sorry.

242
00:13:13,001 --> 00:13:15,378
No, you have nothing to be sorry about.

243
00:13:17,046 --> 00:13:19,507
-You...
-[Minjae] I'm just sorry.

244
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:23,052
No, it's nothing to apologize for, but...

245
00:13:24,095 --> 00:13:25,513
I'm sorry.

246
00:13:34,439 --> 00:13:35,481
[Youseong] Mmm.

247
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:39,944
We're almost done eating,
and he's still not back.

248
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:41,863
I know.

249
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:44,699
They all go missing
whenever they go out to buy tofu.

250
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,452
Call him.

251
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:50,913
Tell him he doesn't need to look for tofu.
Tell him to come back.

252
00:13:51,414 --> 00:13:52,832
Did he take his phone with him?

253
00:13:52,915 --> 00:13:54,792
Yeah, I saw him take it with him earlier.

254
00:14:02,759 --> 00:14:03,885
Right, the tofu.

255
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:06,304
[groans] I left it there.

256
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:12,310
Hello?

257
00:14:12,393 --> 00:14:13,394
Where are you?

258
00:14:14,187 --> 00:14:17,065
Uh... Hurry back home.
We're already done eating.

259
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:19,984
-[Miyoung sighs in relief]
-The tofu?

260
00:14:20,068 --> 00:14:21,235
You lost it?

261
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:23,237
[Miyoung] What? He lost the tofu?

262
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:25,239
That darn tofu.

263
00:14:26,157 --> 00:14:28,493
Tell him to just forget about it
and come back.

264
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:31,913
Hey, Dad says to forget about it
and just hurry back.

265
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:35,792
<i>Just forget it and come home, okay?</i>

266
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:39,212
<i>Hello?</i>

267
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:40,713
Lim Youseong, are you there?

268
00:14:41,631 --> 00:14:42,715
Hello?

269
00:14:43,758 --> 00:14:46,260
What... Are you there or did you hang up?

270
00:14:46,344 --> 00:14:47,595
I'm still here.

271
00:14:48,930 --> 00:14:50,765
Fine. I'll be there soon.

272
00:15:16,791 --> 00:15:18,668
-You're still here.
-Uh...

273
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:20,086
I was about to leave.

274
00:15:20,670 --> 00:15:22,088
I left that here, so...

275
00:15:22,171 --> 00:15:24,257
Yeah. Here. The tofu.

276
00:15:54,829 --> 00:15:57,915
No matter how I look at it,
I just don't think this is okay.

277
00:15:58,875 --> 00:15:59,876
[Minjae] Sorry?

278
00:16:02,545 --> 00:16:04,005
Please stop seeing Youjin.

279
00:16:09,051 --> 00:16:11,387
It's easy to say
it's discrimination or prejudice

280
00:16:12,471 --> 00:16:14,265
when it's not about you.

281
00:16:15,141 --> 00:16:18,144
[sighs] But now that it's my own sister,

282
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:20,521
I just can't get past it.

283
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:25,776
Please stop seeing my sister.

284
00:16:31,574 --> 00:16:35,828
But that's not something you can decide.

285
00:16:36,871 --> 00:16:37,872
What?

286
00:16:37,955 --> 00:16:40,833
And it's not something
I can decide either.

287
00:16:41,417 --> 00:16:43,461
Youjin isn't a kid.

288
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:44,754
She's an adult.

289
00:16:46,422 --> 00:16:48,966
She made the decision for herself,

290
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:51,636
and no one has the right to interfere.

291
00:16:51,719 --> 00:16:52,720
Hmm...

292
00:16:54,138 --> 00:16:55,765
She's not a kid, she's an adult?

293
00:16:56,641 --> 00:16:57,683
Then what about you?

294
00:16:59,185 --> 00:17:01,145
You're even more of an adult than she is.

295
00:17:02,063 --> 00:17:05,274
You're more of an adult, so act like one.

296
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:09,070
If some naive girl says she likes you,

297
00:17:09,153 --> 00:17:11,322
you don't just go,
"Yay, I hit the jackpot!"

298
00:17:12,156 --> 00:17:13,449
You tell her no

299
00:17:14,283 --> 00:17:15,952
and to find someone better.

300
00:17:16,035 --> 00:17:18,746
That's what an adult would do. Am I wrong?

301
00:17:21,749 --> 00:17:24,126
Firstly, Youjin isn't some jackpot.
She's a person.

302
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:25,461
[Youseong] Don't get hung up on words.

303
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:27,463
Why do you keep speaking informally to me?

304
00:17:27,546 --> 00:17:29,674
What if I am?

305
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:33,719
You think I'm in any mood to be polite
in a situation like this, sir?

306
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:39,725
-If you're done, I'm leaving.
-Wait.

307
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:42,812
Do you really like Youjin?

308
00:17:47,858 --> 00:17:50,319
Yes, I really do.

309
00:17:51,862 --> 00:17:54,156
I genuinely like her a lot.

310
00:17:54,865 --> 00:17:57,326
If you like her, you should let her go.

311
00:17:58,160 --> 00:17:59,328
You know what they say.

312
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:02,456
"If you love someone, set them free."

313
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:05,293
You really are selfish, you know.

314
00:18:09,255 --> 00:18:11,591
So you're saying
you really can't break up with her?

315
00:18:12,049 --> 00:18:16,262
[scoffs] Well, as I said,
that's not something I can decide.

316
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:18,639
Well, stop putting it all on her.

317
00:18:18,723 --> 00:18:19,932
I'm not putting it on her.

318
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:23,603
I can't go into every little detail
with you right now,

319
00:18:23,686 --> 00:18:27,023
but Youjin cares about me so much,

320
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:29,150
and she's put so much
into this relationship.

321
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:33,279
After all the love and effort
she's given me,

322
00:18:33,362 --> 00:18:37,617
I owe it to her
to give this everything I've got.

323
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:43,205
Unless her feelings for me change
or she falls for someone else,

324
00:18:43,289 --> 00:18:45,041
I may give up on other things,

325
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:49,086
but I'll never give up on Youjin.

326
00:19:50,398 --> 00:19:52,483
WANT TO LEARN HOW TO PLAY POKER?

327
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:54,068
JUST WATCH THIS!

328
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:55,736
All right, everyone.

329
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:58,155
Here are three tips for playing poker.

330
00:19:58,239 --> 00:20:02,576
<i>First, remember your cards</i>
<i>and your opponent's.</i>

331
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:07,581
<i>And second, keep a close eye</i>
<i>on your opponent.</i>

332
00:20:07,665 --> 00:20:11,877
<i>You want to watch for signs</i>
<i>like darting eyes,</i>

333
00:20:11,961 --> 00:20:16,090
<i>stiff posture, or trembling hands.</i>

334
00:20:16,173 --> 00:20:19,260
<i>Then you can catch them bluffing.</i>

335
00:20:19,969 --> 00:20:21,679
<i>And third...</i>

336
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:57,047
Would you like to bet?

337
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,260
[Chansoo] Half the pot.

338
00:21:03,721 --> 00:21:07,266
Five, four, three, two...

339
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:08,350
[Hangyeol] Call.

340
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:10,519
Call.

341
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:24,283
Would you like to bet?

342
00:21:25,493 --> 00:21:29,538
-Five, four, three, two...
-[Hangyeol sighs heavily]

343
00:21:35,085 --> 00:21:36,086
Fold.

344
00:21:39,590 --> 00:21:40,674
[Chansoo] You're such a coward.

345
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:43,803
I'm not a coward.

346
00:21:43,886 --> 00:21:45,596
I just had a bad hand.

347
00:21:45,721 --> 00:21:49,767
So think it through before you fold.

348
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:52,269
Well, I keep getting lousy hands.

349
00:21:52,353 --> 00:21:53,771
What am I supposed to do?

350
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:54,855
All in.

351
00:21:58,317 --> 00:21:59,693
Don't look away.

352
00:21:59,777 --> 00:22:02,530
Keep your eyes right here.

353
00:22:04,824 --> 00:22:06,617
If you're scared, you can fold.

354
00:22:13,999 --> 00:22:15,584
[Minjae] Are you serious right now?

355
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:18,295
What the hell are you doing?

356
00:22:19,255 --> 00:22:21,715
You're gambling at school? Seriously?

357
00:22:22,299 --> 00:22:24,134
We're not gambling.

358
00:22:24,635 --> 00:22:26,887
We're just having a little fun
on our lunch break.

359
00:22:26,971 --> 00:22:28,013
What's the big deal?

360
00:22:28,681 --> 00:22:29,807
[Chansoo] We're not betting money.

361
00:22:29,890 --> 00:22:30,975
We're betting candy.

362
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:32,184
I don't care what it is.

363
00:22:32,268 --> 00:22:34,520
Who said you could
bring this stuff to school?

364
00:22:38,065 --> 00:22:39,692
A needle thief becomes an ox thief.

365
00:22:39,775 --> 00:22:42,403
You don't notice your clothes
getting wet in a drizzle.

366
00:22:42,987 --> 00:22:45,072
Once you get hooked on this stuff,

367
00:22:45,155 --> 00:22:47,324
it'll ruin your life
and tear your family apart.

368
00:22:47,408 --> 00:22:49,910
Don't you know how dangerous
gambling addiction is?

369
00:22:49,994 --> 00:22:52,162
[mumbling] You don't even have a family...

370
00:22:54,123 --> 00:22:56,083
[chuckling nervously] Sorry.

371
00:22:58,252 --> 00:22:59,503
I'm really sorry.

372
00:22:59,587 --> 00:23:02,798
I mean, this... This would get you
in serious trouble anywhere.

373
00:23:02,882 --> 00:23:04,800
And you actually brought it to school?

374
00:23:05,676 --> 00:23:06,677
Who brought this?

375
00:23:07,303 --> 00:23:08,304
Who was it?

376
00:23:09,013 --> 00:23:11,056
Why did Sejin have to bring this...

377
00:23:12,308 --> 00:23:13,309
Was it you?

378
00:23:15,603 --> 00:23:16,645
I'm sorry.

379
00:23:17,146 --> 00:23:19,815
You get a few compliments,
and now you can do whatever?

380
00:23:19,899 --> 00:23:20,900
No. I'm sorry.

381
00:23:23,903 --> 00:23:24,904
Throw it all out.

382
00:23:25,988 --> 00:23:27,489
-Okay.
-Get rid of it. Now.

383
00:23:32,494 --> 00:23:33,996
[Taeho] Never bring this here again.

384
00:23:46,467 --> 00:23:49,887
Hey, where did Lim Youjin go again,
leaving her seat empty?

385
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:52,389
Right, Youjin said
she needed to study at the library,

386
00:23:52,473 --> 00:23:53,849
so I told her she could go.

387
00:23:55,601 --> 00:23:56,602
Oh...

388
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:58,354
Youjin is the most sensible one here.

389
00:24:02,483 --> 00:24:03,484
[Youjin] Professor.

390
00:24:04,193 --> 00:24:05,194
Yes?

391
00:24:05,861 --> 00:24:07,863
Our genius Professor Talking Hat.

392
00:24:09,782 --> 00:24:11,158
Do you know how to play poker?

393
00:24:12,159 --> 00:24:13,160
No.

394
00:24:13,994 --> 00:24:15,829
[Youjin] Come on, you know how. Teach me.

395
00:24:17,748 --> 00:24:21,085
Poker takes both strategy and luck.

396
00:24:21,877 --> 00:24:24,421
But actually,
it's just a simple game of probability.

397
00:24:25,255 --> 00:24:28,467
If you can do basic math,

398
00:24:28,550 --> 00:24:30,928
even an elementary school kid
can pick it up.

399
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:33,347
What are the odds of drawing an ace first?

400
00:24:35,099 --> 00:24:36,350
1 in 13.

401
00:24:39,269 --> 00:24:40,312
7.7%.

402
00:24:40,396 --> 00:24:41,522
7.7.

403
00:24:44,066 --> 00:24:45,609
If your first card is an ace,

404
00:24:45,693 --> 00:24:49,363
that leaves only three aces
among the remaining 51 cards.

405
00:24:49,446 --> 00:24:54,493
The odds of drawing another ace
are 3 in 51...

406
00:24:56,453 --> 00:24:57,705
which is 5.9%.

407
00:24:57,788 --> 00:24:59,456
Right. 5.9%.

408
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:02,960
That's much lower than your chance
of getting that first ace.

409
00:25:14,013 --> 00:25:16,181
What... how did you do that?

410
00:25:16,265 --> 00:25:18,767
You have to remember every card
to do this.

411
00:25:18,851 --> 00:25:19,852
You have to be smart.

412
00:25:20,978 --> 00:25:22,021
Wow.

413
00:25:23,272 --> 00:25:25,399
I'm saying you can't do it
because you're dumb.

414
00:25:26,942 --> 00:25:29,903
Well, there are plenty
of other poker techniques too,

415
00:25:29,987 --> 00:25:31,447
but when it comes down to it,

416
00:25:32,614 --> 00:25:35,868
the key skill is assessing the situation
to make the right decision,

417
00:25:35,951 --> 00:25:39,246
maximizing your chances
of making the best possible hand

418
00:25:39,329 --> 00:25:43,500
while calculating your opponent's odds,
predicting what they're holding,

419
00:25:43,584 --> 00:25:46,211
and adjusting your strategy accordingly.

420
00:25:47,546 --> 00:25:48,547
Oh.

421
00:25:50,340 --> 00:25:52,760
[hesitates] There must be
a foolproof system.

422
00:25:52,843 --> 00:25:54,303
Like a cheat sheet or something?

423
00:25:55,554 --> 00:25:57,389
You know, I've seen that in movies.

424
00:25:57,473 --> 00:25:59,975
Calculating the odds with an algorithm,
like a computer.

425
00:26:00,059 --> 00:26:01,894
Yeah, I made one in elementary school.

426
00:26:02,770 --> 00:26:04,104
In elementary school?

427
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:06,065
I got bored, so I made one.

428
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:11,195
Then... could I have it?

429
00:26:12,529 --> 00:26:15,115
Think of it as saving my life,
and give it to me. Please?

430
00:26:16,784 --> 00:26:18,202
And what will you do in return?

431
00:26:19,036 --> 00:26:20,037
What?

432
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:23,540
That's three times I've saved you.
And you expect me to do it for free?

433
00:26:24,249 --> 00:26:25,459
Do you have no shame?

434
00:26:26,919 --> 00:26:29,296
Uh... Well, what do you want me to do?

435
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:32,007
Mmm... First,

436
00:26:32,841 --> 00:26:34,259
bow to me three times.

437
00:26:35,219 --> 00:26:36,470
-Bow?
-[Jihoon] Yeah.

438
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:38,514
Bow three times, and be my slave forever.

439
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:40,432
Be your slave forever?

440
00:26:40,516 --> 00:26:43,560
Okay. I was kidding
about the forever part. Just 30 years.

441
00:26:46,814 --> 00:26:47,815
Three years?

442
00:26:47,898 --> 00:26:49,108
No, I can't do that.

443
00:26:49,191 --> 00:26:50,192
It's too long.

444
00:26:50,901 --> 00:26:52,569
We're not done. Where are you going?

445
00:26:52,653 --> 00:26:54,363
I have a class. You should go too.

446
00:26:58,700 --> 00:26:59,701
Aren't you going?

447
00:27:01,328 --> 00:27:04,206
Professor, you're just kidding
about making me your slave.

448
00:27:04,998 --> 00:27:06,792
I told you, I'm not going into math.

449
00:27:06,875 --> 00:27:09,545
I hate memorizing formulas,
and proofs are hard.

450
00:27:10,087 --> 00:27:11,922
Everyone in the department is a genius.

451
00:27:12,005 --> 00:27:14,007
I know I wouldn't have any fun there.

452
00:27:14,091 --> 00:27:15,717
I'd just have a hard time.

453
00:27:19,721 --> 00:27:21,140
Then how about three months?

454
00:27:22,015 --> 00:27:24,393
Just one semester, until we hire a new TA.

455
00:27:24,476 --> 00:27:26,937
Just answer the phone
and run some errands. That's it.

456
00:27:29,940 --> 00:27:31,108
[muttering] 560.

457
00:27:32,442 --> 00:27:35,028
224,848.

458
00:27:36,029 --> 00:27:39,616
Equals 1 over 595.

459
00:27:40,242 --> 00:27:45,998
The answer is 0.16807%.

460
00:27:48,292 --> 00:27:50,043
There. Does that make sense?

461
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:52,462
Well...

462
00:27:53,005 --> 00:27:54,923
If you don't get it, just memorize it.

463
00:27:56,592 --> 00:27:59,219
Uh... Theoretical probabilities
rarely match

464
00:27:59,303 --> 00:28:01,555
what you actually observe in practice.

465
00:28:01,638 --> 00:28:03,682
Or every mathematician
or probability expert

466
00:28:03,765 --> 00:28:05,267
would be getting rich at casinos.

467
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:10,439
The outcome of a game of chance
is also affected by the number of trials.

468
00:28:11,815 --> 00:28:14,276
Maybe that's what they call luck
in this game.

469
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:15,652
Anything else besides luck?

470
00:28:18,322 --> 00:28:19,364
Mind games?

471
00:28:20,324 --> 00:28:21,325
Mind games?

472
00:28:28,707 --> 00:28:33,253
I just sent you the revised slides
and the updated graph.

473
00:28:34,212 --> 00:28:35,297
Okay, I'll take a look.

474
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:42,429
Well done. You can go home now.

475
00:28:42,512 --> 00:28:44,056
Okay. I'll get going.

476
00:28:44,139 --> 00:28:45,140
[Minjae] Okay.

477
00:28:58,487 --> 00:28:59,488
Minjae,

478
00:29:00,405 --> 00:29:04,660
I'm sorry for all the trouble
I caused today.

479
00:29:04,743 --> 00:29:05,744
Okay.

480
00:29:08,664 --> 00:29:12,584
Hey, never bring that stuff
to school again.

481
00:29:19,466 --> 00:29:23,095
The two kinds of people
I hate most are gamblers

482
00:29:25,263 --> 00:29:28,809
and people who make no effort
and leave everything to luck.

483
00:29:29,685 --> 00:29:30,686
Okay.

484
00:29:30,769 --> 00:29:32,896
You see, I've got such high hopes for you.

485
00:29:32,980 --> 00:29:34,606
Don't let me down.

486
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:37,818
Okay, got it.

487
00:29:44,866 --> 00:29:46,743
By the way,

488
00:29:46,827 --> 00:29:48,870
who's giving the presentation for KEIT?

489
00:29:49,538 --> 00:29:51,665
Once you leave,
there won't be anyone to do it.

490
00:29:51,748 --> 00:29:52,749
Is Taeho doing it?

491
00:29:54,001 --> 00:29:56,878
A junior shouldn't handle it
when we have senior members, right?

492
00:29:59,131 --> 00:30:00,215
That...

493
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:04,511
Well, it's not about
being a junior member.

494
00:30:04,594 --> 00:30:05,887
I'm not going to the States.

495
00:30:05,971 --> 00:30:06,972
What?

496
00:30:07,055 --> 00:30:09,850
But you said you were doing your postdoc
in the States.

497
00:30:10,350 --> 00:30:14,229
Well, I can do
my postdoc anywhere and, mmm...

498
00:30:15,313 --> 00:30:17,315
Anyway, I'm not going. I'm staying here.

499
00:30:17,399 --> 00:30:19,568
But the professor said
it's a great opportunity.

500
00:30:19,651 --> 00:30:20,819
Why aren't you going?

501
00:30:20,902 --> 00:30:22,070
It's a great opportunity.

502
00:30:22,154 --> 00:30:23,780
That's just how things turned out.

503
00:30:24,656 --> 00:30:25,782
Yeah.

504
00:30:27,034 --> 00:30:28,410
[Youjin] I'm back.

505
00:30:32,789 --> 00:30:33,790
[whispering] Go.

506
00:30:36,877 --> 00:30:39,004
[Sejin] Library? You seem busy.

507
00:30:39,588 --> 00:30:41,798
Yeah. I was reading papers
on torque sensors.

508
00:30:42,507 --> 00:30:44,176
I'll send my review by tomorrow.

509
00:30:44,259 --> 00:30:45,469
Okay. Thanks.

510
00:30:51,975 --> 00:30:53,518
Do you want to grab dinner?

511
00:30:53,602 --> 00:30:55,437
I have something to tell you too.

512
00:30:56,855 --> 00:30:59,608
Uh, I'm supposed
to see a movie with Subin.

513
00:31:00,275 --> 00:31:01,485
Is it important?

514
00:31:02,194 --> 00:31:03,904
No, not really.

515
00:31:05,405 --> 00:31:07,574
Ah... Then let's do it another day.

516
00:31:07,657 --> 00:31:09,493
Tomorrow? Or the day after.

517
00:31:09,576 --> 00:31:10,786
Any day works for me.

518
00:31:11,536 --> 00:31:13,747
We could do that. Sure. Okay.

519
00:31:15,457 --> 00:31:18,043
I'm late. Sorry, but I have to head out.
I'll call you.

520
00:31:18,126 --> 00:31:19,795
[Minjae] Okay, I'll call you later.

521
00:31:19,878 --> 00:31:21,880
Actually, why don't you call me
when you...

522
00:31:22,798 --> 00:31:24,174
-head home?
-[door closes]

523
00:32:19,104 --> 00:32:20,105
[Sejin] Do you want beer?

524
00:32:20,188 --> 00:32:21,690
-[refrigerator door opens]
-No.

525
00:32:22,190 --> 00:32:24,609
I don't want alcohol clouding my judgment.

526
00:32:41,334 --> 00:32:45,714
Like I said,
we're playing seven-card stud.

527
00:32:47,632 --> 00:32:52,345
Well, it's one hand only,
so we're skipping the betting rounds.

528
00:32:53,263 --> 00:32:55,974
Half pot, double bet, minimum bet,
quarter pot, full pot...

529
00:32:56,057 --> 00:32:57,475
We don't need any of that.

530
00:32:57,559 --> 00:32:59,394
No folding.

531
00:32:59,477 --> 00:33:02,981
We're going all in.

532
00:33:09,905 --> 00:33:10,906
Pick the cards.

533
00:33:11,406 --> 00:33:13,450
The dealer is supposed to pick the cards.

534
00:33:13,533 --> 00:33:14,576
I pick the cards?

535
00:33:14,659 --> 00:33:16,411
You're a player, not the dealer.

536
00:33:17,078 --> 00:33:19,206
What? So you're going to be the dealer?

537
00:33:19,289 --> 00:33:21,583
No, we need someone else.

538
00:33:33,887 --> 00:33:35,096
[Subin] Thank you.

539
00:34:00,330 --> 00:34:01,790
[Subin] Unit 301.

540
00:34:04,542 --> 00:34:06,544
-[doorbell chiming]

541
00:34:10,590 --> 00:34:11,800
-[Youjin] Subin. You made it.
-[Subin] Yeah.

542
00:34:11,883 --> 00:34:12,884
[Youjin] Come in, come in.

543
00:34:14,427 --> 00:34:15,428
What's that?

544
00:34:15,762 --> 00:34:17,847
[Subin] Huh? Ah...

545
00:34:17,931 --> 00:34:20,684
I heard you should bring a gift
when you visit a new home.

546
00:34:21,851 --> 00:34:24,312
-You didn't need to. It's so heavy.
-[Subin chuckles softly]

547
00:34:24,396 --> 00:34:25,397
Hello.

548
00:34:26,314 --> 00:34:27,440
Yes. Hello.

549
00:34:27,524 --> 00:34:28,525
What are you doing?

550
00:34:32,904 --> 00:34:33,905
[Youjin] Oh boy.

551
00:34:33,989 --> 00:34:35,365
-You can sit over there.
-[Subin] Okay.

552
00:34:41,329 --> 00:34:43,123
[Youjin] Did you have trouble
finding the place?

553
00:34:43,206 --> 00:34:44,416
No, I found it right away.

554
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:02,100
CONTACTS

555
00:35:06,062 --> 00:35:08,064
CALLING...
LIM YOUJIN

556
00:35:08,148 --> 00:35:09,316
[automation]<i> The phone is turned off.</i>

557
00:35:09,399 --> 00:35:11,192
<i>-You will now be connected to voicemail...</i>
-[line disconnects]

558
00:35:12,402 --> 00:35:14,571
I thought she was going
to the movies with her.

559
00:35:14,654 --> 00:35:15,739
What's going on now?

560
00:35:16,781 --> 00:35:17,782
Hmm?

561
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:25,665
Let's see.

562
00:35:46,144 --> 00:35:49,397
So the loser buys the winner a meal?

563
00:35:51,608 --> 00:35:54,319
-Yeah, so to speak.
-[Subin] Hmm.

564
00:35:55,111 --> 00:35:58,323
-[Sejin chuckles awkwardly]
-But I've never played poker.

565
00:35:59,324 --> 00:36:00,867
I don't know how to play.

566
00:36:00,950 --> 00:36:03,703
Ah... You're the dealer.

567
00:36:03,787 --> 00:36:05,789
Just hold on to the cards
and then deal them.

568
00:36:05,872 --> 00:36:07,165
Oh.

569
00:36:07,957 --> 00:36:09,334
-Should I pick one?
-[Youjin] Yes.

570
00:36:09,417 --> 00:36:10,418
[Subin] Okay.

571
00:36:19,552 --> 00:36:21,054
-Should I shuffle the cards?
-[Youjin] Yes.

572
00:36:27,268 --> 00:36:30,647
Well, it's one hand only,
so we're skipping the betting rounds.

573
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:34,109
Half pot, double bet, minimum bet,
quarter pot... We don't need any of that.

574
00:36:34,192 --> 00:36:35,944
No folding. We're going all in.

575
00:36:37,278 --> 00:36:38,863
What's half pot and double bet?

576
00:36:38,947 --> 00:36:41,700
Hmm? Ah...
Those are just different bet sizes.

577
00:36:43,868 --> 00:36:45,912
Sorry. I don't know much about poker.

578
00:36:45,995 --> 00:36:48,790
-[Sejin] No, it's okay.
-[Subin chuckling]

579
00:37:04,264 --> 00:37:06,516
-[line connects]
-[automation]<i> The phone is turned off.</i>

580
00:37:06,599 --> 00:37:09,477
<i>-You will now be connected to voicemail...</i>
-[line disconnects]

581
00:37:33,585 --> 00:37:35,670
[softly] Kim Sejin. Where are you?

582
00:37:37,046 --> 00:37:38,381
CONTACTS
KIM SEJIN

583
00:37:38,465 --> 00:37:40,550
CALLING...
KIM SEJIN

584
00:37:40,633 --> 00:37:42,051
[automation]<i> The phone is turned off.</i>

585
00:37:42,135 --> 00:37:43,928
<i>You will now be connected to voicemail.</i>

586
00:37:44,012 --> 00:37:45,805
<i>You will be charged after the tone.</i>

587
00:37:45,889 --> 00:37:47,724
-[beeps]
-[line disconnects]

588
00:37:55,064 --> 00:37:57,817
Now, deal three cards
to each of us, face down.

589
00:37:57,901 --> 00:37:58,902
[Subin] Okay.

590
00:37:59,944 --> 00:38:01,696
No, not like that. One at a time.

591
00:38:01,780 --> 00:38:02,781
One at a time.

592
00:38:05,450 --> 00:38:06,451
[Youjin] Yeah.

593
00:38:19,339 --> 00:38:21,257
Now, deal one card each, face up.

594
00:38:21,341 --> 00:38:22,342
-Face up?
-[Youjin] Yeah.

595
00:38:22,967 --> 00:38:24,260
[Sejin] Oh.

596
00:38:24,344 --> 00:38:25,887
-Here. There you go.
-[Subin] Mmm-hmm.

597
00:38:25,970 --> 00:38:29,432
[Sejin] Here.

598
00:38:30,391 --> 00:38:33,186
Here.

599
00:38:33,269 --> 00:38:35,814
And deal the last card
to each player face down.

600
00:38:35,897 --> 00:38:36,898
Here.

601
00:38:38,191 --> 00:38:39,192
Here.

602
00:38:48,409 --> 00:38:49,494
[Youjin] Hmm.

603
00:38:49,577 --> 00:38:50,954
A royal flush?

604
00:38:53,081 --> 00:38:54,541
What? Are you scared?

605
00:38:56,417 --> 00:38:58,711
A 0.003% chance.

606
00:39:00,463 --> 00:39:01,506
[sighing] Well...

607
00:39:02,507 --> 00:39:04,175
We don't want it to end too quickly.

608
00:39:04,259 --> 00:39:05,593
And it's only the first hand.

609
00:39:07,095 --> 00:39:08,721
How about we allow just one fold?

610
00:39:08,805 --> 00:39:10,265
But it'll cost you a slap. Deal?

611
00:39:10,932 --> 00:39:12,433
What? A slap?

612
00:39:12,517 --> 00:39:14,727
Well, I didn't mean an actual slap.

613
00:39:15,311 --> 00:39:17,021
-I was just joking. Just joking.
-[Subin chuckles softly]

614
00:39:17,105 --> 00:39:18,898
-[Sejin chuckles]
-Just joking.

615
00:39:18,982 --> 00:39:22,151
Is a royal flush a good thing?

616
00:39:22,986 --> 00:39:23,987
[Youjin sighing] Yes.

617
00:39:24,737 --> 00:39:27,031
It's the best hand. It beats everything.

618
00:39:27,574 --> 00:39:29,617
Wow.

619
00:39:30,743 --> 00:39:32,078
Can I see yours too?

620
00:39:32,161 --> 00:39:33,162
Well...

621
00:39:33,246 --> 00:39:35,415
[Youjin] Show her.
She wants to see your cards.

622
00:39:35,498 --> 00:39:37,083
I want to see. Please show me.

623
00:39:46,634 --> 00:39:47,635
[Subin] Hmm.

624
00:39:47,719 --> 00:39:50,346
If Kim Sejin has the ace of hearts,

625
00:39:50,430 --> 00:39:52,599
the royal flush is complete.

626
00:39:53,433 --> 00:39:54,642
Oh.

627
00:39:55,101 --> 00:39:56,436
-Does he have it?
-You little...

628
00:39:57,061 --> 00:39:58,646
I can't tell you that.

629
00:39:58,730 --> 00:40:00,982
Lim Youjin, are you going
to play dirty like this?

630
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:05,528
[sighs] Kim Sejin, you don't have the ace.

631
00:40:08,656 --> 00:40:09,949
Because I've got three.

632
00:40:10,033 --> 00:40:11,242
It's a full house.

633
00:40:11,326 --> 00:40:12,327
[suppressed squeal] Yes!

634
00:40:15,163 --> 00:40:17,332
[chuckling] Yes!

635
00:40:21,878 --> 00:40:24,923
-[Sejin groans]
-[doorbell chiming]

636
00:40:28,051 --> 00:40:30,219
-[Subin] Isn't that Minjae?
-[Youjin shushes]

637
00:40:58,247 --> 00:41:00,750
What the... Those punks.

638
00:41:12,345 --> 00:41:13,721
[softly] But why do we have to hide?

639
00:41:15,139 --> 00:41:16,849
I can't explain right now. Sorry.

640
00:41:17,350 --> 00:41:18,351
[whispering] I'm sorry.

641
00:41:18,434 --> 00:41:19,435
[whispering] It's okay.

642
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:21,854
Hey, Kim Sejin.

643
00:41:21,938 --> 00:41:25,441
I won the game, so you're handing in
your resignation at the lab next week

644
00:41:25,525 --> 00:41:26,985
and going back to Daejeon, okay?

645
00:41:27,068 --> 00:41:28,695
Are you serious, though?

646
00:41:28,778 --> 00:41:29,821
[Youjin] Yes, I am.

647
00:41:29,904 --> 00:41:31,197
That was the deal.

648
00:41:31,280 --> 00:41:33,408
He's going to quit the lab and leave?

649
00:41:33,491 --> 00:41:34,492
[Youjin] Yeah.

650
00:41:35,076 --> 00:41:37,620
He said he'd quit and leave
if he lost the poker game.

651
00:41:38,204 --> 00:41:39,205
[Subin] No way.

652
00:41:39,288 --> 00:41:40,957
Who would bet that on a poker game?

653
00:41:41,040 --> 00:41:42,041
[Youjin] Exactly.

654
00:41:42,125 --> 00:41:43,918
It was his idea to do this bet.

655
00:41:44,002 --> 00:41:45,253
That's how crazy he is.

656
00:41:45,878 --> 00:41:48,256
Hey, don't go back on your word.

657
00:41:48,339 --> 00:41:49,590
You promised.

658
00:41:50,967 --> 00:41:52,260
-[doorbell chiming]
-[Sejin grunts]

659
00:41:52,343 --> 00:41:53,344
Hey! [shushes]

660
00:41:53,428 --> 00:41:55,304
-[doorbell chiming]
-[Sejin whispering] Turn it off.

661
00:41:57,515 --> 00:41:59,517
Hey, I know you guys are in there.

662
00:42:00,059 --> 00:42:01,644
You better come open this door.

663
00:42:02,603 --> 00:42:05,314
If you don't open this door
by the time I count to three,

664
00:42:05,398 --> 00:42:07,942
you guys are going to be
in serious trouble. Huh?

665
00:42:10,987 --> 00:42:15,324
Three, two, one.

666
00:42:38,222 --> 00:42:42,685
The three of you turned off the lights,
locked the door, and were hiding.

667
00:42:44,979 --> 00:42:46,689
What were you three doing in here?

668
00:42:50,443 --> 00:42:51,694
Are you going to answer me?

669
00:42:57,075 --> 00:42:58,076
Jung Subin.

670
00:42:59,077 --> 00:43:00,078
[Subin] Yes.

671
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:01,412
[Minjae] You tell me.

672
00:43:02,288 --> 00:43:04,290
You were supposed
to see a movie with Youjin.

673
00:43:04,373 --> 00:43:05,500
What are you doing here?

674
00:43:13,049 --> 00:43:14,717
You guys were fighting again, right?

675
00:43:16,219 --> 00:43:18,805
Were you throwing punches?
Pulling each other's hair?

676
00:43:18,888 --> 00:43:20,181
You had an MMA match?

677
00:43:20,264 --> 00:43:21,724
No, it's not like that.

678
00:43:22,725 --> 00:43:24,310
We were playing cards.

679
00:43:26,479 --> 00:43:27,563
Playing cards?

680
00:43:37,365 --> 00:43:39,075
You can play cards at home.

681
00:43:41,661 --> 00:43:42,995
But why did you hide?

682
00:43:43,079 --> 00:43:45,498
That, I'm not sure.

683
00:43:46,332 --> 00:43:48,042
Were you guys playing for money?

684
00:43:48,126 --> 00:43:49,794
No, we weren't playing for money.

685
00:43:51,420 --> 00:43:53,214
-It wasn't money, but...
-[Minjae] Then what is it?

686
00:43:58,970 --> 00:44:00,847
If Sejin lost,

687
00:44:00,930 --> 00:44:03,683
he'd quit the lab and go back to Daejeon.

688
00:44:12,733 --> 00:44:14,235
Kim Sejin, Jung Subin, get up.

689
00:44:21,367 --> 00:44:24,537
But... I didn't initiate it.

690
00:44:24,620 --> 00:44:27,456
Uh... It was Kim Sejin's idea to play.

691
00:44:27,999 --> 00:44:29,000
She's right.

692
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:32,378
Youjin didn't do anything wrong.

693
00:44:33,546 --> 00:44:36,215
This was all my fault,
and I take full responsibility.

694
00:44:37,425 --> 00:44:41,512
[sighs heavily] I should've treated
my only lab mate better, but I failed to.

695
00:44:42,054 --> 00:44:45,183
I guess that caused
some misunderstandings, and here we are...

696
00:44:46,475 --> 00:44:48,895
I'll accept whatever punishment
you give me.

697
00:44:48,978 --> 00:44:52,273
I'll take a good look at myself
and reflect on what I've done.

698
00:44:52,356 --> 00:44:55,568
What, you're going to take a good look
at yourself and reflect? You?

699
00:44:56,152 --> 00:44:57,153
Hey.

700
00:44:59,530 --> 00:45:02,909
If you want me to go to Daejeon, I will.

701
00:45:04,327 --> 00:45:07,079
If you want me to quit the lab, I will.

702
00:45:07,163 --> 00:45:09,665
I'll do whatever you say.

703
00:45:10,750 --> 00:45:12,001
Okay. Fine.

704
00:45:12,084 --> 00:45:13,502
[groaning] Oh, come on.

705
00:45:13,586 --> 00:45:16,172
Kim Sejin is just faking it
to not go to Daejeon.

706
00:45:16,881 --> 00:45:19,008
Hey, you're real clever.

707
00:45:19,091 --> 00:45:20,259
You're so sneaky.

708
00:45:20,343 --> 00:45:22,386
Hey, did I say you could get up?

709
00:45:22,470 --> 00:45:25,306
Well, I didn't do anything wrong.
Why do I have to kneel?

710
00:45:25,389 --> 00:45:26,974
You didn't do anything wrong?

711
00:45:27,516 --> 00:45:30,436
I didn't do anything wrong.
Who are you to treat me like this?

712
00:45:30,519 --> 00:45:32,230
Even my parents wouldn't do this.

713
00:45:32,313 --> 00:45:34,482
Yeah? You're proud of what you've done?

714
00:45:34,565 --> 00:45:36,317
Is that why you're talking back to me?

715
00:45:36,901 --> 00:45:37,902
I'm just saying,

716
00:45:39,111 --> 00:45:41,656
Kim Sejin made the bet in the first place.

717
00:45:42,240 --> 00:45:43,950
If I won, he'd go back to Daejeon,

718
00:45:44,033 --> 00:45:46,285
and if he won,
I'd have to break up with you.

719
00:45:48,246 --> 00:45:50,414
Playing poker was his idea, too.

720
00:45:50,498 --> 00:45:53,209
And now that I actually won,
he's going back on his word.

721
00:45:57,129 --> 00:45:58,130
[Minjae] Hey, Lim Youjin.

722
00:46:00,549 --> 00:46:01,550
Come with me.

723
00:46:09,558 --> 00:46:10,685
Hey, wait up.

724
00:47:13,080 --> 00:47:14,373
What are you doing?

725
00:47:15,750 --> 00:47:17,126
Why did you throw your jacket?

726
00:47:17,209 --> 00:47:18,627
I'm the one who should be mad.

727
00:47:19,378 --> 00:47:21,005
So you think what you did was okay?

728
00:47:22,006 --> 00:47:24,300
[sighs] How many times
do I have to tell you?

729
00:47:24,383 --> 00:47:26,177
I told you, he started the fight.

730
00:47:27,386 --> 00:47:29,722
You just

731
00:47:30,389 --> 00:47:33,100
bet our relationship on a card game. Huh?

732
00:47:35,019 --> 00:47:38,272
I know you're young and immature,
but how could you do that?

733
00:47:39,690 --> 00:47:40,983
If you had lost the game,

734
00:47:41,067 --> 00:47:43,194
were you actually
going to break up with me?

735
00:47:43,819 --> 00:47:44,862
But I won.

736
00:47:44,945 --> 00:47:46,030
[Minjae chuckling] "But I won?"

737
00:47:46,530 --> 00:47:47,823
What if you had lost?

738
00:47:49,200 --> 00:47:50,368
I didn't lose.

739
00:47:50,451 --> 00:47:53,537
Even if I had, I wouldn't break up
over this. Isn't that obvious?

740
00:47:53,621 --> 00:47:55,956
[loudly] I'm saying it's not obvious!

741
00:47:59,502 --> 00:48:01,379
All right. I'm sorry.

742
00:48:01,462 --> 00:48:02,546
[Minjae] All right?

743
00:48:03,422 --> 00:48:05,049
What's all right?

744
00:48:06,592 --> 00:48:07,593
You...

745
00:48:09,011 --> 00:48:12,390
Is everything just easy,
just a joke to you?

746
00:48:13,140 --> 00:48:14,600
[Youjin] What are you saying?

747
00:48:14,683 --> 00:48:16,685
When did I say everything was a joke?

748
00:48:16,769 --> 00:48:19,772
You just bet our relationship on a game,

749
00:48:19,855 --> 00:48:22,525
like it's no big deal,
like it's all just a joke!

750
00:48:22,608 --> 00:48:23,609
Am I wrong?

751
00:48:23,692 --> 00:48:25,945
You're the one who treats me
like I'm no big deal.

752
00:48:26,779 --> 00:48:27,780
[Minjae] What?

753
00:48:28,364 --> 00:48:31,075
You made me kneel, yelled at me,
and even threw your jacket.

754
00:48:31,951 --> 00:48:35,037
You treated me with zero respect
just because I like you more.

755
00:48:35,121 --> 00:48:37,373
That's because you did something wrong.

756
00:48:37,873 --> 00:48:40,960
Even if I did, you don't treat someone
you care about like that.

757
00:48:41,627 --> 00:48:43,587
Then don't give me a reason to be mad.

758
00:48:46,465 --> 00:48:48,175
This is seriously messed up.

759
00:48:49,677 --> 00:48:51,637
I chose someone who doesn't love me back,

760
00:48:51,720 --> 00:48:53,347
so I can somehow live with that.

761
00:48:54,807 --> 00:48:57,184
Being falsely blamed
and misunderstood really sucks.

762
00:49:00,020 --> 00:49:01,313
I guess I lost after all.

763
00:49:02,606 --> 00:49:03,607
What?

764
00:49:05,359 --> 00:49:06,986
What do you mean, you lost?

765
00:49:07,069 --> 00:49:08,195
-Hey.
-[Youjin] I'm going to go.

766
00:49:08,279 --> 00:49:09,280
[Minjae] Hey!

767
00:49:17,371 --> 00:49:18,581
Hey, let me take you home.

768
00:49:18,664 --> 00:49:19,915
I can get home by myself.

769
00:49:19,999 --> 00:49:21,750
I'll take you home. What's wrong?

770
00:49:21,834 --> 00:49:22,835
[Youjin] I said I'm okay.

771
00:49:24,753 --> 00:49:26,547
You... You said you lost earlier.

772
00:49:26,630 --> 00:49:28,007
What did you mean?

773
00:49:29,133 --> 00:49:31,886
What did you mean by that? Huh?

774
00:51:23,706 --> 00:51:24,832
[automation]<i> The phone is turned off.</i>

775
00:51:24,915 --> 00:51:26,709
<i>You will now be connected to voicemail.</i>

776
00:51:26,792 --> 00:51:28,419
<i>You will be charged after the tone.</i>

777
00:51:31,005 --> 00:51:33,007
-[line disconnects]

778
00:52:07,499 --> 00:52:08,500
Minjae.

779
00:52:08,584 --> 00:52:09,585
[Minjae] Yeah?

780
00:52:09,668 --> 00:52:11,962
Professor Ahn wants you in his office.

781
00:52:12,046 --> 00:52:14,923
But he seems a little... upset.

782
00:52:16,091 --> 00:52:18,093
Oh. Right, okay.

783
00:52:19,553 --> 00:52:20,554
[Taeho] Okay.

784
00:52:24,933 --> 00:52:27,102
What's up? Did something bad happen?

785
00:52:27,603 --> 00:52:28,979
[Taeho] Ah. Well, no. Nothing bad...

786
00:52:31,440 --> 00:52:33,067
[sighs] Is it bad?

787
00:52:33,984 --> 00:52:34,985
[Chansoo] What?

788
00:52:35,569 --> 00:52:38,113
[Taeho] There was a postdoc position
in the States,

789
00:52:38,197 --> 00:52:39,531
but Minjae turned it down.

790
00:52:40,282 --> 00:52:42,159
-[Hangyeol] What?
-[Chansoo] Minjae did his PhD in Korea,

791
00:52:42,242 --> 00:52:43,577
so he needs a postdoc abroad.

792
00:52:45,496 --> 00:52:48,207
Well, he could go into industry.

793
00:52:48,290 --> 00:52:50,292
It looked like he had other plans in mind.

794
00:52:55,964 --> 00:52:59,009
Well, they asked you about your schedule,

795
00:53:00,719 --> 00:53:03,055
so I told them you're done
with your dissertation

796
00:53:03,138 --> 00:53:05,057
and just need to wrap things up

797
00:53:06,058 --> 00:53:07,309
and defend it.

798
00:53:07,393 --> 00:53:08,560
[Minjae] Yes.

799
00:53:08,644 --> 00:53:10,145
Everything just fell into place.

800
00:53:10,229 --> 00:53:11,897
Why did you turn it down?

801
00:53:12,690 --> 00:53:13,691
Well...

802
00:53:14,525 --> 00:53:16,402
I don't think I'm ready yet.

803
00:53:16,485 --> 00:53:18,112
Ready for what?

804
00:53:18,195 --> 00:53:19,905
All you had to do was go.

805
00:53:22,032 --> 00:53:24,034
It's a rare opportunity, you know.

806
00:53:24,660 --> 00:53:25,661
But

807
00:53:26,453 --> 00:53:28,247
I could do a postdoc here, too.

808
00:53:28,956 --> 00:53:32,501
And getting a job at a research institute
in Korea wouldn't be bad either.

809
00:53:32,584 --> 00:53:35,671
You said you eventually
wanted to teach at a university.

810
00:53:36,588 --> 00:53:38,507
Now you're getting a research job
in Korea?

811
00:53:39,508 --> 00:53:43,178
I'm thinking maybe getting a job
wouldn't be so bad.

812
00:53:43,804 --> 00:53:45,055
Is there...

813
00:53:46,098 --> 00:53:48,559
something going on
that I don't know about?

814
00:53:48,642 --> 00:53:49,643
What?

815
00:53:49,727 --> 00:53:52,855
[Jaehong] I heard you had a rough time
when your leg got inflamed before.

816
00:53:52,938 --> 00:53:54,815
Is something wrong with your health?

817
00:53:56,191 --> 00:53:58,485
No, that's not what this is about.

818
00:53:59,570 --> 00:54:01,321
I just... I just want

819
00:54:01,780 --> 00:54:03,574
to keep my options open.

820
00:54:07,453 --> 00:54:09,580
Why do you think
he suddenly decided not to go?

821
00:54:12,291 --> 00:54:13,500
Did something happen?

822
00:54:14,543 --> 00:54:16,670
Does he want to go to a different country?

823
00:54:17,463 --> 00:54:18,672
What do you think it is?

824
00:54:19,381 --> 00:54:20,716
[Jihoon] Go ask him yourself.

825
00:54:22,509 --> 00:54:23,635
I can't right now.

826
00:54:23,719 --> 00:54:25,053
Things are a little tense.

827
00:54:25,137 --> 00:54:26,555
[Jihoon] Isn't it actually a good thing?

828
00:54:27,723 --> 00:54:28,724
What?

829
00:54:29,433 --> 00:54:32,478
[Jihoon] It's "out of sight, out of mind,"
as they say.

830
00:54:32,561 --> 00:54:34,855
You'd rather have him close
than be apart, right?

831
00:54:36,940 --> 00:54:38,484
Yeah, I would.

832
00:54:38,567 --> 00:54:40,152
I would, but still...

833
00:54:42,946 --> 00:54:45,866
There's no way he decided not to go
because of me, right?

834
00:54:46,700 --> 00:54:47,993
[Jihoon] Would you like it if he did?

835
00:54:48,535 --> 00:54:49,745
No.

836
00:54:49,828 --> 00:54:50,954
[Jihoon] Why not?

837
00:54:51,038 --> 00:54:53,040
He's giving up on his dream for you.

838
00:54:53,123 --> 00:54:54,791
That shows how much he loves you.

839
00:54:57,461 --> 00:54:59,296
What if he regrets it later?

840
00:55:01,548 --> 00:55:05,677
He could regret giving up on his dream
because of me and resent me for it.

841
00:55:05,761 --> 00:55:07,638
Then that's just how small a man he is.

842
00:55:07,721 --> 00:55:09,431
And that's just how much he cared.

843
00:55:16,688 --> 00:55:17,689
What?

844
00:55:18,732 --> 00:55:20,567
You have a weird habit, you know.

845
00:55:21,527 --> 00:55:23,403
What habit? I don't have any habits.

846
00:55:23,487 --> 00:55:24,488
You do.

847
00:55:24,571 --> 00:55:26,323
You try to do other people's homework.

848
00:55:27,115 --> 00:55:29,535
Why do you keep trying
to make his decisions for him?

849
00:55:30,744 --> 00:55:33,997
He gets to make his own decisions,
and he's responsible for them.

850
00:55:34,081 --> 00:55:37,292
You just look at your own feelings,
and make your own decisions.

851
00:55:37,376 --> 00:55:38,460
Do your own homework.

852
00:55:41,755 --> 00:55:44,675
I can't tell if you get it
or if you're just nodding along.

853
00:55:45,384 --> 00:55:46,385
I got it.

854
00:55:46,468 --> 00:55:47,469
[Jihoon] No, you didn't.

855
00:55:48,178 --> 00:55:51,431
And hey, you should
say all this to him, not me.

856
00:55:51,515 --> 00:55:52,683
Talk to him directly.

857
00:55:52,766 --> 00:55:54,935
Why do you bring your drama to me?
I'm busy.

858
00:55:56,562 --> 00:55:58,021
You always find it entertaining.

859
00:55:58,105 --> 00:55:59,648
Entertaining, my ass. Now go.

860
00:56:32,514 --> 00:56:33,515
[Youjin] You're late.

861
00:56:35,017 --> 00:56:36,018
I'm right on time.

862
00:56:37,019 --> 00:56:38,186
[Youjin] But I got here earlier.

863
00:56:43,025 --> 00:56:44,818
Right. You should order a drink.

864
00:56:44,901 --> 00:56:45,944
[Minjae] I'm good.

865
00:56:46,028 --> 00:56:47,529
I need to head back soon anyway.

866
00:56:48,822 --> 00:56:50,073
Why did you want to see me?

867
00:56:52,117 --> 00:56:54,077
I had something to ask you...

868
00:56:56,204 --> 00:56:57,748
about your postdoc in the States.

869
00:56:57,831 --> 00:56:59,625
[Minjae] Let me ask you something first.

870
00:57:00,584 --> 00:57:02,502
When you said you lost, what did you mean?

871
00:57:03,253 --> 00:57:04,254
[Youjin] What?

872
00:57:04,338 --> 00:57:06,923
You said that it really sucks
and that you lost.

873
00:57:08,050 --> 00:57:09,384
What did you mean by that?

874
00:57:11,553 --> 00:57:13,555
[mumbling] When I said that...

875
00:57:16,266 --> 00:57:17,934
I was really upset,

876
00:57:18,018 --> 00:57:19,394
so I can't really remember.

877
00:57:21,063 --> 00:57:22,230
You can't remember?

878
00:57:22,731 --> 00:57:24,983
I mean, I don't remember the exact words,

879
00:57:25,734 --> 00:57:26,818
but I kind of remember.

880
00:57:26,902 --> 00:57:27,944
So tell me.

881
00:57:28,028 --> 00:57:29,237
What did you mean?

882
00:57:32,407 --> 00:57:34,076
It meant I was really upset.

883
00:57:36,286 --> 00:57:37,496
"I lose.

884
00:57:37,579 --> 00:57:38,664
"You win.

885
00:57:39,164 --> 00:57:40,290
"Good for you.

886
00:57:40,374 --> 00:57:42,000
"You're so great."

887
00:57:42,084 --> 00:57:43,168
That's what it means.

888
00:57:48,256 --> 00:57:49,966
Did it mean anything else?

889
00:57:51,176 --> 00:57:52,177
What?

890
00:57:54,346 --> 00:57:55,347
So...

891
00:57:56,682 --> 00:57:58,058
you didn't mean

892
00:57:59,768 --> 00:58:01,895
you wanted to break up, or stop seeing me?

893
00:58:02,479 --> 00:58:03,814
That's not what I meant.

894
00:58:08,944 --> 00:58:11,196
I mean, couples fight sometimes.

895
00:58:12,155 --> 00:58:14,074
Do we have to break up
every time we fight?

896
00:58:15,409 --> 00:58:16,702
No, of course not.

897
00:58:18,870 --> 00:58:20,497
[inhales sharply] Minjae,

898
00:58:21,164 --> 00:58:23,083
have you really never dated before?

899
00:58:23,166 --> 00:58:24,167
[chuckling] What?

900
00:58:28,130 --> 00:58:29,798
Well, actually, more importantly,

901
00:58:31,091 --> 00:58:34,094
what happened with that postdoc
in the States?

902
00:58:34,177 --> 00:58:35,303
Oh, that.

903
00:58:36,513 --> 00:58:38,306
I don't need to go.

904
00:58:41,435 --> 00:58:44,312
Is it... because of me?

905
00:58:48,400 --> 00:58:49,484
I'm fine with it.

906
00:58:50,610 --> 00:58:52,612
I told you, I can wait a year or so.

907
00:58:53,155 --> 00:58:54,281
I'm not fine with it.

908
00:58:54,364 --> 00:58:55,949
I don't want to be away from you.

909
00:58:57,701 --> 00:58:59,661
[Youjin] I can't go to the States, though.

910
00:58:59,745 --> 00:59:00,996
That's why I'm not going.

911
00:59:03,498 --> 00:59:04,666
I just...

912
00:59:06,293 --> 00:59:07,878
want to do my best for you.

913
00:59:11,715 --> 00:59:14,217
How is giving up on your dreams
doing your best?

914
00:59:18,054 --> 00:59:21,558
You don't have to choose
between your dream and love.

915
00:59:25,687 --> 00:59:26,688
It's only a year.

916
00:59:28,482 --> 00:59:30,317
We'll be together again next spring.

917
00:59:33,653 --> 00:59:34,821
I'll be right here,

918
00:59:35,906 --> 00:59:38,033
and I'll be an even better person by then.

919
01:00:45,517 --> 01:00:47,561
I'VE BEEN
DYING TO SEE YOU!

920
01:00:47,644 --> 01:00:49,646
WELCOME

921
01:01:39,529 --> 01:01:43,450
BETWEEN STEPS

922
01:01:43,533 --> 01:01:45,869
[Subin] <i>Is Youjin seeing someone?</i>

923
01:01:45,952 --> 01:01:48,204
Because I missed you so much.

924
01:01:48,288 --> 01:01:49,998
I met Park Minjae there.

925
01:01:50,081 --> 01:01:52,667
[Youjin] <i>I pray that the woman he likes</i>
<i>brutally dumps him</i>

926
01:01:52,751 --> 01:01:54,044
<i>and leaves him in tears.</i>

927
01:01:54,127 --> 01:01:56,338
[Hangyeol] Minjae's coming back to Korea
after his postdoc.

928
01:01:56,713 --> 01:02:00,050
Did you tell Minjae
to break up with Youjin?

929
01:02:01,927 --> 01:02:05,597
[Minjae] <i>If there's anything on your mind,</i>
<i>let it all out.</i>

930
01:02:07,682 --> 01:02:09,100
<i>You're making the right choice.</i>
